From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tarik0 <22205836+tarik0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:46:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] uvm: only flush the bottom half queues that exist

The bottom half queue is only created for GPUs with replayable faults. On others
uvm_suspend() flushed a zeroed queue, a NULL dereference with the queue spinlock held
that hangs the suspend. The open modules don't support such GPUs, but the code is shared
with the R580 driver.

Upstream PR 1340 (tarik0). Fixes upstream issue 1212. Added the same guard to
uvm_parent_gpu_flush_bottom_halves(), which has the same problem when a GPU is released
and its parent stays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_global.c  | 3 ++-
 kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu_isr.c | 7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_global.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_global.c
index f17d806c..185d3ef3 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_global.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_global.c
@@ -339,7 +339,8 @@ static NV_STATUS uvm_suspend(void)
 
         uvm_parent_gpu_set_isr_suspended(gpu->parent, true);
 
-        nv_kthread_q_flush(&gpu->parent->isr.bottom_half_q);
+        if (gpu->parent->isr.replayable_faults.handling)
+            nv_kthread_q_flush(&gpu->parent->isr.bottom_half_q);
 
         if (gpu->parent->isr.non_replayable_faults.handling)
             nv_kthread_q_flush(&gpu->parent->isr.kill_channel_q);
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu_isr.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu_isr.c
index 48f4b541..e5113fa2 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu_isr.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu_isr.c
@@ -452,8 +452,11 @@ NV_STATUS uvm_parent_gpu_init_isr(uvm_parent_gpu_t *parent_gpu)
 
 void uvm_parent_gpu_flush_bottom_halves(uvm_parent_gpu_t *parent_gpu)
 {
-    nv_kthread_q_flush(&parent_gpu->isr.bottom_half_q);
-    nv_kthread_q_flush(&parent_gpu->isr.kill_channel_q);
+    if (parent_gpu->isr.replayable_faults.handling)
+        nv_kthread_q_flush(&parent_gpu->isr.bottom_half_q);
+
+    if (parent_gpu->isr.non_replayable_faults.handling)
+        nv_kthread_q_flush(&parent_gpu->isr.kill_channel_q);
 }
 
 void uvm_parent_gpu_disable_isr(uvm_parent_gpu_t *parent_gpu)
